1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Most AI job tools give you a score and ask you to trust it. JobPilot makes every career decision inspectable.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:35,000
JobPilot is local-first and evidence-first. Gemma 4 12B is the primary semantic model, while deterministic code calculates every score.

3
00:00:35,000 --> 00:01:05,000
This public demo uses only synthetic data. Browse six fictional roles, search by title or company, and filter by work mode or evidence sufficiency.

4
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Every required and preferred capability stays tied to the source requirement, candidate evidence, match class, uncertainty, and exact point allocation.

5
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Experience is calculated month by month. Work mode and travel remain visible constraints and never silently change technical points.

6
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:58,000
The Score Receipt reconciles one hundred visible points. See a Score Change recomputes the affected capability and creates a new receipt hash.

7
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:20,000
GPT-5.6 Terra is reserved for complex strategy and critique. This no-key result is clearly prepared, and GPT-5.6 never generates the score.

8
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The Trust Lab shows Gemma primary, deterministic scoring, fixture reliability, optional GPT, privacy, proof, and Codex's Build Week contribution.

9
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:50,000
JobPilot: know why a job fits before you apply.
